v 3
d ifpriquaids: censored QUAIDS demand estimation pipeline
d
d A suite of Stata commands for estimating censored Quadratic Almost Ideal
d Demand Systems by the Shonkwiler-Yen two-step method, and for turning the
d estimates into observation-level elasticities.
d
d The commands run as a pipeline:
d
d   ifpriwl          Working-Leser model for all food (stage 1)
d   ifpriprobit      first-stage probits giving the cdf and pdf
d   ifpriquaids      censored QUAIDS, flexible in the number of goods
d   ifpriquaidselas  conditional expenditure and price elasticities
d   ifpriunc         unconditional elasticities by multi-stage budgeting
d   ifpripost        posts elasticity summaries so the chain can be
d                    bootstrapped for standard errors
d
d Homogeneity and symmetry are imposed by construction; adding-up is
d relaxed by default and available through an option.  The first-stage
d probits are kept separate from the demand system so that their
d specification, exclusion restrictions and sample stay under the user's
d control.
d
d Requires Stata 14 or later.
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260826
d
d Author: Andrew Comstock, IFPRI
d Support: email a.comstock@cgiar.org
d
f ifpriwl.ado
f ifpriwl.sthlp
f ifpriprobit.ado
f ifpriprobit.sthlp
f ifpriquaids.ado
f ifpriquaids.sthlp
f nlsurifpriquaids.ado
f ifpriquaidselas.ado
f ifpriquaidselas.sthlp
f ifpriunc.ado
f ifpriunc.sthlp
f ifpripost.ado
f ifpripost.sthlp
f _ifpriclean.ado
f ifpriquaids_example.do
f ifpri_bootstrap_template.do
